.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-455-# of the ADR-103 hold produced a dirty tree, then a commit made AFTER the
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-456-# preflight proved CI green, which `tag()` then signed. That commit was also
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh:457:# invisible to the pair-rail step 15 (none of the four files is in
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh:458:# `pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt`). Two independent defenses now:
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-459-#   1. the same-tree predicate below (four oracles) short-circuits the phase;
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-460-#   2. the writer skips each stamp line whose version is already the target.
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-461-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-462-_oracle() {
